---
orbit 2026
component PromoBanner
settings {
  heading: Text = "Free shipping on orders over 75" label "Heading"
  layout: Select("left", "center", "right") = "center" label "Alignment"
  accent: Color = #1a73e8 label "Accent colour"
  padding: Range(0, 64, step: 8) = 24 label "Vertical padding"
  showBadge: Toggle = true label "Show the badge"
}
---
{# A merchant-configurable component. `settings` is a reserved binding: the
   engine types it from the frontmatter block, so `settings.layout` is the
   string-literal union "left" | "center" | "right", not String — a typo in a
   comparison is a compile error, not a silently-false branch.

   Note what is NOT here: `style="..."` with an interpolation. Style attributes
   are static-only (O1095), because a string in a CSS declaration position can
   close the declaration and open another.

   `--promo-accent={settings.accent}` is the one carve-out, and it is narrow:
   a static property name, and a value whose type has a lexical form the engine
   can enumerate completely. A Color is exactly six hex digits, so the sink can
   refuse everything else rather than try to escape it — and it revalidates at
   emission rather than trusting the type. `padding` stays a data-* attribute
   because a Range is a finite set the stylesheet can enumerate. #}
<aside
  class="promo promo--{settings.layout}"
  --promo-accent={settings.accent}
  data-padding={settings.padding}
>
  <if {settings.showBadge}><span class="promo__badge">Offer</span></if>
  <p class="promo__text">{settings.heading}</p>
  {# `<match>` is where that union pays off. There is no default arm, and that
     is deliberate: a default would absorb a fourth alignment added next year,
     and this component would quietly render the wrong hint for it. Without one,
     adding an option to the Select fails the check right here, by name. #}
  <match {settings.layout}>
    <case "left">
      <p class="promo__hint">Left-aligned text keeps the badge on the same line.</p>
    </case>
    <case "center">
      <p class="promo__hint">Centred layouts hide the secondary line on mobile.</p>
    </case>
    <case "right">
      <p class="promo__hint">Right-aligned text reverses the badge order.</p>
    </case>
  </match>
</aside>
